`tool.execution_progress` was only trace-logged, so an MCP server's status
messages never reached the client. Route them through the same
`_meta.progressMessage` channel Codex uses, so both providers behave the same.

The message stays out of the tool call's content, repeats are coalesced, and
the action is only emitted while the tracked call is Running, which is the one
status in which the reducer applies a content change. `tool.execution_partial_result`
is untouched: that carries the tool's real output and keeps streaming to its
terminal resource.
