From 3f9a954792bf2dca868e9315a34a2db0ed2a6832 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:39:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] copilot: cover tool progress across an MCP authentication
 pause

The running-state gate had no test for the pause it exists to handle. Emit
progress while the call sits in AuthRequired, resolve authentication, then emit
the same message again: it must be published the second time, which only holds
because the paused message was never recorded as last sent.

Without that, a message the reducer discarded would still count as sent and the
valid repeat would be coalesced away, leaving the status line stuck.
